          "title": "You'll want to know: 重",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "重 — zhòng — \"heavy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "这个太重了 zhège tài zhòng le — This one is too heavy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 重 (zhòng) — a short fall and a long bar on top, and under them 里, its vertical running up through the bar. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "重 (zhòng) is inherited from Middle Chinese drjowngX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), glossed 'much', 'thick' and 'careful'. 'Heavy' is not among the glosses, so the step to it is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
